WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.184
Build the kernel from three waves.

00:00:02.184 --> 00:00:06.921
Lesson five, Bandtlow’s Lemma one point eight, gives the one-sided ladder.

00:00:06.921 --> 00:00:12.617
For degree two, the first three frequencies are minus three, minus five, and minus seven.

00:00:12.617 --> 00:00:17.695
Each coloured arrow turns clockwise and adds one term to the kernel approximation.

00:00:17.695 --> 00:00:24.608
Its length is the real coefficient sigma multiplied by the outer radius to the negative frequency index.

00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:27.333
The gold tip follows the finite sum.

00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:29.172
Select a pair of frequencies.

00:00:29.172 --> 00:00:34.506
Multiply the three-term sum by its complex conjugate and the squared boundary speed.

00:00:34.506 --> 00:00:41.824
Row three and column five select a product with amplitude c three times c five and phase twice the angle.

00:00:41.824 --> 00:00:47.179
The speed squared has a constant wave and two waves with frequencies plus and minus two.

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:49.654
The minus two wave cancels this pair’s phase.

00:00:49.654 --> 00:00:54.150
Its constant contribution survives averaging over the full circuit.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.564
Three diagonals survive a full turn.

00:00:56.564 --> 00:01:01.557
The main diagonal contributes a positive multiple of each squared amplitude.

00:01:01.557 --> 00:01:06.187
Each adjacent cell contributes minus one quarter of a neighbouring product.

00:01:06.187 --> 00:01:08.663
The reflected cell makes a second copy.

00:01:08.663 --> 00:01:16.642
For three terms, subtract about zero point zero one zero zero five from zero point zero six nine nine four.

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:22.381
The resulting zero point zero five nine eight nine is the energy of the three-term packet.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:26.343
Adding further kernel terms changes this finite energy.

00:01:26.343 --> 00:01:28.737
Turn the exact identity into a bound.

00:01:28.737 --> 00:01:36.311
For the full ladder, every surviving coefficient is nonnegative, so discarding the subtracted correction gives an upper bound.

00:01:36.311 --> 00:01:37.933
Each sigma is at most two.

00:01:37.933 --> 00:01:45.678
Squaring the radial factors makes the remaining geometric sum decrease by a factor of R to the minus four at every step.

00:01:45.678 --> 00:01:48.686
Its sum gives the explicit constant C two of R.

00:01:48.686 --> 00:01:53.139
Bandtlow’s Lemma one point ten follows by taking the square root.

